From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the idle clock hears every key

The desk locked under somebody typing. The compositor's idle clock hears
only the input the shell forwards to its windows, and a key typed into a
browser window or into the shell's own page is forwarded nowhere.

- `StartDeskActivity` (`chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_desk_activity.cc`)
  observes `ui::UserActivityDetector`, which sees every event the platform
  dispatches and skips aura's synthesized mouse moves.
- It tells `DeskActivity` (`components/domicile/browser/desk_activity.cc`),
  and each control channel sends the compositor `activity`.
- Started in `PostBrowserStart`, beside the shell windows.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
 chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc
index 0555c38..f7d7fa1 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 
 #include "chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_command_socket.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_desk.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_desk_activity.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_file_dialogs.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_shell_windows.h"
 #include "components/domicile/browser/desktop_prefs.h"
@@ -1779,6 +1780,12 @@ void ChromeBrowserMainParts::PostBrowserStart() {
   // somebody will want to point `load_shell` at.
   domicile::StartShellWindows();
 
+  // Domicile's engine fork: every input event, to the compositor's idle clock,
+  // which hears only what the shell forwards to its windows. Here because the
+  // platform's event source exists by now, and it is the browser process's
+  // input rather than any page's.
+  domicile::StartDeskActivity();
+
   for (auto& chrome_extra_part : chrome_extra_parts_) {
     chrome_extra_part->PostBrowserStart();
   }
